  "notes": "Two tabs, joined by a pair of link planes: light leaving the laser table through its link arrives on the experiment table through the partner. On the laser table a long-pass dichroic (edge 800 nm) transmits a 1064 nm laser and reflects a 532 nm one onto the same line. On the experiment table one lens focuses both; the screen at the green focus shows the infrared a little out of focus (chromatic focal shift) and larger, since the 1064 nm laser has M² = 1.3. Switch tabs at the top of the bench."
